  "type": "title",
  "name": "Menu",
  "notes": "The first screen. It loads the saved progress (which monsters are unlocked, the best times, the last pick) and counts how many of the 9 monsters have won a classic run (cleared), then the MONSTER SURVIVAL logo drops in over the meadow and bounces twice, a white flash, then the monster picker appears. Left / Right browse 18 entries in a loop: the 9 monsters for the classic run, then the same 9 again for the waves mode (no label: past Pebbulk the list simply starts over with Furrbit for the waves mode, and the arrows turn red). Each entry shows its own best time above the monster (the fastest won run of that monster in that mode). START begins the run with it: the classic run (scn_run) or the waves run (scn_waves). In the classic list the first 3 monsters (Furrbit, Emberpup, Splashell) are playable at first and the first won run of each monster unlocks the next one; the waves entries all stay locked (dark silhouettes, WIN WITH ALL 9 MONSTERS) until every one of the 9 monsters has won a classic run, then all 9 open at once. A save from an older version with fewer than 3 unlocked is raised to 3. SELECT asks whether to clear the saved progress (unlocks and best times). Coming back from a run, the last pick is still selected.",
